a1-chip.notes:
Audit of a1-chip (die, mesh, shire and minion), read-only. Work scripts are in /home/yaroslavvb/claude/work/chip-check-1014/audit/a1-chip-work/.

1. Expected fixes. All 34 findings and the 5 Codex items (T02, T05, T09 and I05 implemented; T03 covered) landed as written or in equivalent words. I checked the sources (git diff), the generated facts (facts.json and ladder-data.json, compared with HEAD) and the after crawl. The drawing fixes are confirmed on the after screenshots:
- scale-060 and scale-078: the two crossings;
- scale-061 and scale-087: the link bit and the mesh hop;
- scale-062: the shire's lane label;
- scale-071: the UC block;
- scale-083: die.metal, now 5 rows;
- scale-046: the register-file note;
- flow-1-stage-2: the miss leaves on lane 2, PA[12:11].
I checked the claims I could against primary evidence: PRM p.18 (rendered), p.36, p.275, p.306, p.309 and p.328; Neighborhood MAS p.18-19 and p.39-40; Shire Cache Specification p.6 and p.11; the DLL document; RTL (shirecache_mesh_master.sv, pvt_defines.vh, rf_latch_2r_1w and intpipe_rf, vpu_tensorb_rf and vpu_lane, et_clk_gate.v, vcfifo_wr_lov_ss.v); noc_esr.h; report.json; the raw info.err DRAM sizes. One wording problem is in new_errors: mesh.no-counters says more about the bridge counters than noc_esr.h shows. Remark on in.mesh.link.4: its 0.42-0.53 pF/mm is the lab's dally_gap.py convention (C = 4E/V^2 on all data-dependent energy, 1-bits included), not wire transitions alone. That is defensible, but it is not the 0.22 pF/mm per-transition figure the finding's truth computed.

